[Music]  a second set of human remains were found  at lake mead yesterday this comes a week  after a man's body was found in a barrel  on the lake shore last sunday madison  kimbrough joins us in the newsroom  tonight with the latest in the  investigation madison sasha two sisters  who were paddle boarding near colville  bay saturday afternoon stumbled across  what they thought was a large rock in  the sand but upon further inspection  they realized it was a human skull along  with other human remains the park  rangers then responded to the scene and  set up a perimeter right now the clark  county coroner's office is working to  identify the remains today i spoke to a  retired henderson police officer david  kohlmeyer he tells us he spoke to the  two sisters and says he doesn't believe  the new remains have any relation to the  body found in a barrel  i believe it's four or five miles away  from the other location so it is a  different location from where the body  the barrel is located so again i do  believe it's a different spot i  definitely was surprised now it makes  you start thinking right like how many  other bodies will be recovered  if they found one in a barrel and one in  another area like how many bodies are  out there now  cole meyer and his partner are offering  five thousand dollars to those who find  additional bodies at the lake he says he  hopes the incentive brings hope and a  sense of closure to the families and  friends of these victims while assisting  local law enforcement in their efforts  and coming up later in our newscast  experts at the mop museum weigh in on  the remains found in a barrel in the  newsroom madison kimbrough live local  now

